WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.267
AutoTokenizer and AutoModelForSequenceClassification make the inference process explicit.

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:12.207
The checkpoint name identifies a DistilBERT model already fine-tuned on sentiment data.

00:00:12.207 --> 00:00:19.162
We load the tokenizer and model from the same checkpoint so their vocabulary and learned parameters match.

00:00:19.162 --> 00:00:23.272
The tokenizer converts the sentence into PyTorch tensors.

00:00:23.272 --> 00:00:28.577
Passing those tensors into the model returns an output object containing logits.

00:00:28.577 --> 00:00:32.862
Logits are raw scores before converting them into probabilities.

00:00:32.862 --> 00:00:38.147
If we wanted the predicted class, we could apply softmax and choose the highest value,

00:00:38.147 --> 00:00:42.522
or use the model configuration to map class IDs to labels.

00:00:42.522 --> 00:00:47.407
This lower-level workflow is useful when you need batching, device control, custom post-processing,

00:00:47.407 --> 00:00:49.232
or access to the internal outputs.

00:00:49.232 --> 00:00:51.997
Notice that we are still doing inference.

00:00:51.997 --> 00:01:00.064
The model weights are not being updated simply because we loaded the model and passed text through it.
